update public.company_faq set answer = $qd$The 3% fee is the customer reveal fee: 3% of the value of the quote you choose, with no cap. A customer pays it once to unlock the identity and contact details of their chosen supplier. It is the platform's main charge and it is paid by the customer — suppliers pay no commission. Nothing is added for paying by card, and the amount is shown in full before payment. No VAT is charged on the reveal fee. Nothing is added for paying by card, and the amount is shown in full before payment. No VAT is charged on the reveal fee.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '89' and md5(answer) = '2484f784c25f6e9ccb24614775739a3f'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: The card processing fee is added on top, and both are shown in full before payment. | The card processing fee is added on top, and both are shown in full before payment. | card processing fee is added | card processing fee is added
update public.agent_knowledge set content = $qd$PRICING & FEES - LIVE, AUTO-SYNCED FROM pricing_config (authoritative; OVERRIDES any pricing figure stated elsewhere). Customer REVEAL FEE: 3% of the accepted quotation value (NO cap, NO discount, NO promotional rate, NO coupon and NO free reveal - the founder's decision of 6 Sep 2026, enforced by a pricing_config constraint), paid by the customer to unlock their chosen supplier. The customer pays the 3% and nothing more: there is NO card processing fee on top (Cabinet Resolution 66/2023 Art. 5(3)); QuotesDone absorbs the Stripe fee as its own expense. The amount is shown in full before payment. QuotesDone is NOT VAT registered: NO VAT is charged on the reveal fee - never say the fee is VAT-inclusive or that VAT is added. Suppliers pay NO commission on won jobs. Supplier registration is FREE for the first 1000 verified registrations, and those 1000 suppliers are exempt PERMANENTLY. Every registration after them pays a yearly subscription of AED 1,000. There is NO calendar start date and there will not be one: charging begins with registration number 1001, whenever that happens. Never state a date, never ask the founder for one. CATEGORY OPENING: a category is OPEN once it has 10 verified registered suppliers (public.v_category_open); matching an RFQ still needs at least one confirmed supplier. Non-response window: 5 working days from the customer's payment - if a revealed supplier stays silent through the chase and the CEO's final call, EVERYTHING the customer paid (the reveal fee) is refunded and QuotesDone bears the Stripe fee; the supplier is charged the exact amount refunded, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14) + an AED 500 administrative fee + simple interest at 12% a year (or the maximum lawful rate) from the due date, and is blocked from matching until paid. There is NO 2% fee and NO supplier commission - never quote those. (Auto-updated 2026-09-14 11:19 UTC.)$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '279' and md5(content) = '9b4123ea15a2786e930d55440e4f0532'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: (reveal fee + card processing fee) | + card processing fee
update public.support_knowledge set body = $qd$These rules come from the signed Terms (texts of 14 Sep 2026, which supersede older wording) and must be stated exactly.

The Reveal Fee: the customer pays 3% of the value of the quotation they select, calculated on the value before VAT, with no cap, once per reveal, by card or Apple Pay. Card-processing charges are added on top so that QuotesDone nets the full 3%; the breakdown is shown to the customer before they pay. There is no VAT on the Reveal Fee, because QuotesDone is not VAT-registered. Comparing quotations is free; the fee arises only when the customer chooses to reveal a supplier.

Supplier response after reveal: the supplier must respond to the customer within 5 working days of the reveal. QuotesDone chases the supplier at 3 working days with the customer copied. On day 5 the CEO seat makes a final call. If the supplier is still silent, the customer's payment is refunded in full automatically, with no request needed, and the supplier owes a non-response charge under the Terms (the refunded amount plus an AED 500 administrative fee (AED 250 for a supplier whose accepted Supplier Agreement is v12 or earlier) and 12% a year simple interest).

Refunds: a refund means everything the customer paid, the 3% and the processing charge; QuotesDone absorbs the processor's fee. The CEO seat approves every refund and verifies each step of the money movement. Support investigates, explains and keeps the customer informed, but never promises a refund before approval, except the automatic non-response refund, which the Terms guarantee.

Never say: that suppliers pay commission (they do not); that VAT is charged on the fee; that a refund needs a form when the supplier did not respond; or any supplier's tax registration number, which is hidden from customers.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where record_id = 'customer_support:company-hard-rules-fees-refunds' and md5(body) = '7c542819b1e6f9c74cb579712c56134a'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: Card-processing charges are added
-- support_knowledge#customer_support:company-hard-rules-fees-refunds@ar: only a wording finding, rewrite by hand -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  وتُضاف رسوم معالجة البطاقة
-- support_knowledge#customer_support:company-pricing@ar: only a wording finding, rewrite by hand -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  وتُضاف رسوم معالجة البطاقة
-- support_knowledge#customer_support:ecommerce-law-14-2023: only a wording finding, rewrite by hand -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: and the card-processing charge
-- support_knowledge#customer_support:ecommerce-law-14-2023@ar: only a wording finding, rewrite by hand -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: رسوم معالجة البطاقة المضافة
update public.support_knowledge set body = $qd$Federal Decree-Law No. 50 of 2022 promulgating the Commercial Transactions Law came into force on 2 January 2023 and repealed Federal Law No. 18 of 1993. It governs dealings between traders: commercial contracts, obligations of merchants, commercial agency, payment instruments and banking operations. Most dealings between a company buyer and a contractor or supplier on QuotesDone are commercial transactions under this law, with the new Civil Code filling gaps.

One rule customers raise: per a law-firm summary, Article 88 entitles a creditor to interest on a commercial debt from the date it falls due unless the parties agreed otherwise, and compound interest is prohibited; the rate and details were not read from the primary text in this pass and are not established here.

Support rules: disputes about payment for work, late payment between customer and supplier, or interest claims are between those two parties under their own contract; QuotesDone facilitates communication (see the dispute resolution ladder) but does not adjudicate or calculate interest. The non-response charge in our Terms (refunded amount plus an AED 500 administrative fee (AED 250 for a supplier whose accepted Supplier Agreement is v12 or earlier) and 12% a year simple interest) is a contractual term between the supplier and QuotesDone, not an application of Article 88; do not describe it as statutory.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where record_id = 'customer_support:commercial-transactions-law-50-2022' and md5(body) = '615f72360be704ba47aa67e69fcd8bd9';
-- support_knowledge#customer_support:company-pricing: only a wording finding, rewrite by hand -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: Card-processing charges are added
update public.support_knowledge set body = $qd$Under the signed Terms (texts of 14 Sep 2026, superseding earlier wording), a supplier whose details a customer has revealed must respond to that customer within 5 working days of the reveal. This is the most important clock support runs, because a silent supplier after the customer has paid is the fastest way to lose the customer's trust.

The sequence, exactly:
1. Day 0: the reveal. Both parties are notified; the supplier receives the customer's details through the platform.
2. Working day 3: if the supplier has not responded, QuotesDone chases the supplier, with the customer copied, stating the reveal reference, the deadline date and time in UAE time, and that non-response triggers a refund and a charge under the Terms.
3. Working day 5: the CEO seat makes the final call on the evidence.
4. If the supplier is still silent, the customer's payment is refunded in full automatically, with no request needed: the 3% fee and the processing charge. The supplier then owes a non-response charge under the Terms (the refunded amount, plus an AED 500 administrative fee (AED 250 for a supplier whose accepted Supplier Agreement is v12 or earlier) and 12% a year simple interest).

Before bidding stage (a different situation): suppliers invited to quote on a request are not charged for declining. A clear decline with a reason (capacity, out of scope, unclear specification) is useful; incomplete quotations are held with notes, never rejected.

If a supplier disputes the charge, investigate with records: was the reveal notice delivered, was the chaser sent on day 3, did the supplier contact the customer by any channel, was there a platform incident? If our notices failed, recommend reversal to the accountant and CEO seats.

Tone: businesslike and non-punitive. "The customer revealed your quotation for QD-1234 on Monday; the response period ends Monday 13 October, 17:00 UAE time. A short call or message to the customer today closes this."$qd$, embedding_gte = null where record_id = 'customer_support:supplier-non-response' and md5(body) = '80b01640e713b06f6c3015833d98e290';
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$PRICING & FEES - LIVE, AUTO-SYNCED FROM pricing_config (authoritative; OVERRIDES any pricing figure stated elsewhere). Customer REVEAL FEE: 3% of the accepted quotation value (NO cap, NO discount, NO promotional rate, NO coupon and NO free reveal - the founder's decision of 6 Sep 2026, enforced by a pricing_config constraint), paid by the customer to unlock their chosen supplier. The customer pays the 3% and nothing more: there is NO card processing fee on top (Cabinet Resolution 66/2023 Art. 5(3)); QuotesDone absorbs the Stripe fee as its own expense. The amount is shown in full before payment. QuotesDone is NOT VAT registered: NO VAT is charged on the reveal fee - never say the fee is VAT-inclusive or that VAT is added. Suppliers pay NO commission on won jobs. Supplier registration is FREE for the first 1000 verified registrations, and those 1000 suppliers are exempt PERMANENTLY. Every registration after them pays a yearly subscription of AED 1,000. There is NO calendar start date and there will not be one: charging begins with registration number 1001, whenever that happens. Never state a date, never ask the founder for one. CATEGORY OPENING: a category is OPEN once it has 10 verified registered suppliers (public.v_category_open); matching an RFQ still needs at least one confirmed supplier. Non-response window: 5 working days from the customer's payment - if a revealed supplier stays silent through the chase and the CEO's final call, EVERYTHING the customer paid (the reveal fee) is refunded and QuotesDone bears the Stripe fee; the supplier is charged the exact amount refunded, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14) + an AED 500 administrative fee + simple interest at 12% a year (or the maximum lawful rate) from the due date, and is blocked from matching until paid. There is NO 2% fee and NO supplier commission - never quote those. (Auto-updated 2026-09-14 11:19 UTC.)$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '177872' and md5(content) = '9b4123ea15a2786e930d55440e4f0532'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: (reveal fee + card processing fee) | + card processing fee
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$## [Financial] What is the 3% fee?
The 3% fee is the customer reveal fee: 3% of the value of the quote you choose, with no cap. A customer pays it once to unlock the identity and contact details of their chosen supplier. It is the platform's main charge and it is paid by the customer — suppliers pay no commission. Nothing is added for paying by card, and the amount is shown in full before payment. No VAT is charged on the reveal fee. Nothing is added for paying by card, and the amount is shown in full before payment. No VAT is charged on the reveal fee.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '174480' and md5(content) = '32bad374ad1e146c7ee13d676e6ea38e'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: The card processing fee is added on top, and both are shown in full before payment. | The card processing fee is added on top, and both are shown in full before payment. | card processing fee is added | card processing fee is added

